  "notes": "Receipt state for L0, L2, and the ReleaseGate observation is an in-memory store with reserve/commit/cancel/holders_of/release_section. DisclosureStore was not opened and MySQL was not started. L0 is one process lock around decide-and-commit, with no rollback and no event identity; the two case-6 processes do not share that lock. L1 is one stdlib sqlite3 BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction that re-reads policy and receipts, then commits or rolls back. Its receipt identity is a surrogate receipt_id, the same kind of identity DisclosureStore uses, not an event key. L2 checks one shared monotonic policy version at commit and does not lock or roll back a multi-receipt write. Shared failures: ['duplicate_event', 'retry_after_commit']. Candidate event_key is L1 plus UNIQUE(event_id, resource_id, unit_id) and an in-transaction replay check. That is a small variant of L1, not a new mechanism, so the verdict is ANALYZE when that residual is real. numeric_thresholds_met=True. dev scan 5 seeds, 8 subjects, 4 assets. formal=false. E9/E10: no frozen definition in this checkout.",
